## Phase A plan round 4 (revision) - redesigned cross-check, found suggested fix was ALSO wrong

Round-3's suggested fix (full-struct-equality-modulo-4-exceptions) was itself
found wrong by a NEW probe measurement (P3): the shipped HostSetup.tsx UI
lets a host legitimately set starting_life to any value, commander_damage_
threshold to any value >=1, and FreeForAll's deck_size to 40 (looser than
the built-in Minimum(60)) - none of these are in the suggested exception
list, so whole-struct equality would reject real, currently-working host
customization. Redesigned into a 4-verdict-per-field classification instead
of a same/different binary:
  Locked (must equal built-in - no host control exists, e.g. min/max_players,
    singleton, command_zone, range_of_influence, custom_rules)
  NoLooserThan (equal-or-stricter only, for every axis with a serde(default)
    fallback: supplies_fixed_deck, sideboard_policy [via a new private
    permissiveness-order helper, twin of DeckCopyLimit::permits_no_more_than],
    default_deck_copy_limit)
  Derived (uses_commander checked against ITS OWN payload's command_zone +
    commander_damage_threshold, not against the built-in - so a host who
    retunes the threshold passes while a payload that flips the flag without
    flipping its sources fails)
  HostChoice (never compared - starting_life, deck_size, commander_damage_
    threshold's value itself, archenemy_player, allow_debug_actions - genuine
    per-room/per-session choices the product already ships)

