## Phase A plan round 4 review - REJECT, 4 blockers (deck_size gap is severe)

Blocker 1: max_players is host-mutated at SUBMISSION TIME (HostSetup.tsx:473,
"max_players: playerCount" - not a setLocalFormatConfig call, which is why
the round-4 measurement method missed it). Locked would break the shipped
host flow for any host picking fewer than the format ceiling (the common
case). min_players confirmed genuinely never client-written, stays Locked.
Fix: reclassify max_players as NoLooserThan (payload <= built_in, >=
min_players). Measurement method itself flagged as needing to become
"every field where FORMAT_DEFAULTS[f] differs from the onHost payload", not
"every setLocalFormatConfig call site" - the latter structurally can't see
submission-time spreads.

Blocker 2 (MOST SERIOUS): deck_size classified HostChoice leaves the
phase's OWN headline security goal unmet - and this phase specifically
converts deck_size from trusted-derived (via FormatConfig::for_format(..)
.expect(..).deck_size, 3 of the 7 .expect() sites being deleted) into
payload-sourced, while simultaneously marking it completely unchecked. A
minimal forgery (Commander's Exactly(100) -> Minimum(1), every other field
exactly the built-in) passes all 17 verdicts. The plan's own P5 fixture only
got caught because it also tampered with 3 OTHER axes - V11's claim that
"the rejection cites axes that actually bind" was masking this gap rather
than exposing it. Reviewer showed the "unchecked or nothing" dichotomy is
false: the real host surface is tightly bounded and measurable (FreeForAll-
only picker, exactly 2 options, variant-preserving edit, rehydration
rejects a variant change) - fix is a bounded verdict: Locked on the
DeckSizeRule variant (kills Exactly->Minimum swaps), NoLooserThan or an
enumerated per-format allowed-value-set on the count.

Blocker 3: the Derived verdict for uses_commander is not airtight - checks
only the CONJUNCTION (uses_commander == command_zone && threshold.is_some()),
not presence, so a forger can null commander_damage_threshold AND flip
uses_commander off simultaneously and both remain internally consistent.
Read 5x in deck_validation.rs. V5 only tests the raising direction; the
lowering direction passes untested. Fix: pin threshold's PRESENCE to Locked
(.is_some() must match the built-in), leave the contained VALUE as
HostChoice (matches what the shipped picker actually allows).

Blocker 4 (architectural): D1 (migrate the whole cross-check into
FormatConfig::deserialize's general-purpose ingress) is INCOHERENT as
designed - the HostChoice/Locked classification encodes LOBBY-UI PRODUCT
POLICY (literally measured from HostSetup.tsx), not a type-level invariant;
FormatConfig::deserialize is the general ingress for save files, replays,
PersistedGameState, WASM boundary, AND P2P per its own docstring, and
cannot distinguish "a host submitting a request" from "the engine reloading
already-adjudicated state" - migrating the Locked verdicts there would
break reload of persisted games (e.g. max_players holding the actual seat
count, archenemy_player holding actual seating assignment). Fix: split D1
into D1a (self-consistency invariants true of every FormatConfig everywhere
- the Derived check, custom_rules.is_none() - safe to migrate to the general
deserializer) and D1b (registry-comparison admission policy - Locked/
NoLooserThan - stays at the admission gate PERMANENTLY, never migrates).
D3 (sideboardPolicyForFormat echo) needs its own landing phase since it
depended on D1's now-retracted "falls out automatically" claim.

Non-blocking: sideboard_policy_permits_no_more_than's match arms were never
actually written out in the plan text (only described in prose) - must be
included verbatim next round. Recurrence-gap/D2 deferral confirmed
proportionate ONCE blockers 1-3 are fixed (residual truly-unread HostChoice
set shrinks to starting_life/threshold-value/archenemy_player/
allow_debug_actions, each verified 0 reads in deck_validation.rs).

